&lt;p>The wayfinding model is
described in &lt;a href="https://pedestriandynamics.org/pyFDS-Evac/models/visibility/">Visibility and cognitive maps&lt;/a>
: sign
legibility through smoke, and the per-agent cognitive map it feeds. The ideas
behind it, with figures, are in the
&lt;a href="https://pedestriandynamics.org/pyFDS-Evac/docs/understanding/concepts/#wayfinding">Wayfinding section of Concepts&lt;/a>
. The
&lt;a href="https://pedestriandynamics.org/pyFDS-Evac/models/verification/testing-familiarity/">familiarity routing verification&lt;/a>
checks that fully familiar and discovering agents behave differently.&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>